---
title: Panfried scallops with white wine garlic sauce
description: Panfried scallops with white wine garlic sauce is an easy and delicious recipe, perfect for a date night in. Served with risotto, it's a showstopper.
image: https://simply-delicious-food.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/White-wine-garlic-scallops-4.jpg
cuisine: American
tags: How to cook scallops, Panfried scallops, Scallop recipes
prep time: 10 minutes
author: Alida Ryder
cook time: 10 minutes
source: https://simply-delicious-food.com/panfried-scallops-with-white-wine-garlic-sauce/#recipe
course: Dinner
time required: 20 minutes
nutrition:
  calories: 193 kcal
  fat: 8 g
  saturated fat: 2 g
  carbohydrates: 7 g
  sugar: 1 g
  protein: 16 g
  fiber: 1 g
  sodium: 1076 mg
  serving size: 4 people (scallops only)
servings: 4
---

Heat a large, non-stick #frying pan{} over high heat.

Pat @scallops{500%g} dry with paper towels. Drizzle with @olive oil{1%tbsp} and season with @salt{1%tsp} and @pepper{1/2%tsp}.

Add the scallops to the hot pan (do this in batches to avoid overcrowding the pan) and allow to panfry for ~{2-3%minutes} per side until they are golden brown and seared on both sides.

Remove from the pan and set aside.

Melt @butter{2%tbsp} in the pan then add @garlic{3-4%cloves}(minced). Allow to cook for ~{30%seconds} then pour in @white wine{1/2%cup}((I used Chardonnay)), @lemon juice{1%tsp} and @parsley{2%tbsp}(finely chopped).

Bring the sauce to a simmer then cook for ~{3-5%minutes} until the sauce has reduced slightly.

Add the scallops back into the pan and allow to heat through.

Serve with sides of your choice, such as lemon risotto and crusty bread.
